

;; Package kernel runs processes under the box's kernel on amd64 (doc/go/PROCESS-SPEC.md, KU1):
;; the amd64 mechanics in a test guest. A process is a second TamaGo runtime at ring 3, in its own
;; address space, isolated from the kernel (the box's program at ring 0) by the MMU, talking to the
;; kernel by system calls that are the doorbell's call block one level down (§1). KU1 is the
;; mechanics: per-process page tables (text/rodata shared, data/bss/heap/stacks private), the GDT/
;; TSS/SYSCALL set-up and the ring-3 entry (board.UserSetup, board.EnterUser), a SYSCALL served, a
;; fault that ends the process, a nil dereference that becomes the process's own panic, and a CR3
;; switch between two processes of one image.
;;
;; b1 (§2.1, S6): one image is the kernel and every process. The kernel enters a process at
;; whim_uentry (board.UEntryAddr); the process's data and bss are at the kernel's virtual
;; addresses for them but in the process's own private pages, so each process has its own page
;; tables. The kernel's own mappings are present in every process's tables but supervisor-only, so
;; the crossing code (board's sysentry and fault path) runs at ring 0 with the process's tables
;; loaded until it switches CR3 (§2.1, no KPTI, KS7).
;;
;; KU1 runs on amd64 only (§9, K9); arm64 is KU3. This package builds only for tamago/amd64.
(in-ns 'go.arbace.box.kernel) (go/file "kernel.go" :build ["//go:build amd64"] :doc "Package kernel runs processes under the box's kernel on amd64 (doc/go/PROCESS-SPEC.md, KU1):\nthe amd64 mechanics in a test guest. A process is a second TamaGo runtime at ring 3, in its own\naddress space, isolated from the kernel (the box's program at ring 0) by the MMU, talking to the\nkernel by system calls that are the doorbell's call block one level down (§1). KU1 is the\nmechanics: per-process page tables (text/rodata shared, data/bss/heap/stacks private), the GDT/\nTSS/SYSCALL set-up and the ring-3 entry (board.UserSetup, board.EnterUser), a SYSCALL served, a\nfault that ends the process, a nil dereference that becomes the process's own panic, and a CR3\nswitch between two processes of one image.\n\nb1 (§2.1, S6): one image is the kernel and every process. The kernel enters a process at\nwhim_uentry (board.UEntryAddr); the process's data and bss are at the kernel's virtual\naddresses for them but in the process's own private pages, so each process has its own page\ntables. The kernel's own mappings are present in every process's tables but supervisor-only, so\nthe crossing code (board's sysentry and fault path) runs at ring 0 with the process's tables\nloaded until it switches CR3 (§2.1, no KPTI, KS7).\n\nKU1 runs on amd64 only (§9, K9); arm64 is KU3. This package builds only for tamago/amd64.\n" :imports [


    ^{:line 23} [binary "encoding/binary"]
    ^{:line 24} [errors "errors"]

    ^{:line 26} [abi "arbace/box/abi"]
    ^{:line 27} [board "arbace/box/board"]])


