^{:go/end 352} (go/method winBytes "winBytes is the n bytes at the process's virtual address va, through the kernel alias of the\nprocess's RAM (§2.1, §4.3): the window (its heap and stack), or its private data+bss. The kernel\nnever dereferences a user VA; it reads and writes the process's memory at the kernel's own\naddress for the same physical page (one subtraction after a bounds check).\n" [^{:tag (* Proc)} p ^uintptr va ^int64 n] :results [(slice byte) bool]
